[Event "Modern Benoni"]

{The Benoni gives up central space for a queenside majority and an active g7-bishop.}
1. d4 {Centre. The pawn on d4 controls e5.}
1... Nf6 {Flexible. The knight on f6 controls d5 and e4.}
2. c4 {Space. The pawn on c4 controls d5.}
2... c5 {[%cal Gc5d4] The Benoni. The pawn on c5 eyes the pawn on d4.}
3. d5 {Gains space.}
3... e6 {Opens lines. The pawn on e6 eyes the pawn on d5.}
4. Nc3 {Develops. The knight on c3 controls e4.}
4... exd5 {Takes. The pawn on d5 eyes the pawn on c4 and controls e4.}
5. cxd5 {Recaptures.}
5... d6 {Solid. The pawn on d6 controls e5.}
6. e4 {Centre.}
 (6. Nf3 {Develops. The knight on f3 controls d4 and e5.}
6... g6 {Fianchetto.}
7. g3 {Fianchetto.}
7... Bg7 {Develops.}
8. Bg2 {Long diagonal.}
8... O-O {Castles. The king is safe and the rook comes into play.}
9. O-O {Castles. The king is safe and the rook comes into play.}
9... Na6 {Heads for c7.}
)
6... g6 {Fianchetto.}
7. Nf3 {Develops. The knight on f3 controls d4 and e5.}
 (7. f4 {The Taimanov. The pawn on f4 controls e5.}
7... Bg7 {Develops.}
8. Bb5+ {Checks. It is check, so the reply is forced.}
8... Nfd7 {Blocks. The knight on d7 controls e5.}
9. a4 {Stops ...a6 and ...b5.}
)
7... Bg7 {Develops.}
8. Be2 {Develops.}
8... O-O {Castles. The king is safe and the rook comes into play.}
9. O-O {Castles. The king is safe and the rook comes into play.}
9... Re8 {Hits e4. The rook on e8 eyes the pawn on e4 and controls e5.}
 (9... a6 {Prepares ...b5.}
10. a4 {Stops ...b5.}
)
10. Nd2 {Supports e4.}
10... Na6 {Heads for c7.}
 (10... Nbd7 {Heads for e5. The knight on d7 controls e5.}
